{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00161",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.9,
      "end_seconds": 2.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Hello again. Come on in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.19,
      "end_seconds": 5.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Thanks. Sorry, I'm a little early."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 9.63,
      "end_seconds": 14.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.18,
      "end_seconds": 21.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together. Right, in your own words, what's happened?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.99,
      "end_seconds": 30.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.75,
      "text": "I'm here because of pain low in the pelvis. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.08,
      "end_seconds": 33.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.09,
      "end_seconds": 41.15,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "I've had it for three weeks. Oh, and bloating. That's been about the same, ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.53,
      "end_seconds": 45.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.26,
      "end_seconds": 56.2,
      "duration_seconds": 9.94,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, pretty moderate, if I'm being honest. Oh, and pain around my period. That's been about the same, six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.74,
      "end_seconds": 63.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.85,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.98,
      "end_seconds": 67.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "It's mild, honestly. Honestly, on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.37,
      "end_seconds": 71.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Have you had a lot of tiredness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.32,
      "end_seconds": 74.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.85,
      "end_seconds": 77.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Has there been any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.31,
      "end_seconds": 79.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "No, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.92,
      "end_seconds": 83.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Right, have you had any vomiting or bleeding between periods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.07,
      "end_seconds": 86.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.51,
      "end_seconds": 90.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Right, what about burning when passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.13,
      "end_seconds": 95.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any burning when passing urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 99.03,
      "end_seconds": 104.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice burning when passing urine. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.93,
      "end_seconds": 111.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "So, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.27,
      "end_seconds": 117.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.15,
      "end_seconds": 120.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.6,
      "end_seconds": 123.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.5,
      "end_seconds": 126.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.83,
      "end_seconds": 130.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.65,
      "end_seconds": 133.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.44,
      "end_seconds": 136.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.95,
      "end_seconds": 139.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Just a C-section, about ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.65,
      "end_seconds": 144.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.43,
      "end_seconds": 150.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "My mother had high blood pressure. My sister has thyroid problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.19,
      "end_seconds": 154.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 155.91,
      "end_seconds": 163.01,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "She is on Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.22,
      "end_seconds": 170.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "I'd been on allopurinol, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.61,
      "end_seconds": 178.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.99,
      "end_seconds": 194.56,
      "duration_seconds": 15.57,
      "text": "Gout, for nearly five years. I have an underactive thyroid, for five years. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.87,
      "end_seconds": 198.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "I see. Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.64,
      "end_seconds": 206.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.26,
      "end_seconds": 226.94,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 97 percent on room air, blood pressure 116 over 74, heart rate 77, temp 36.8 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.61,
      "end_seconds": 228.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.99,
      "end_seconds": 233.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.88,
      "end_seconds": 239.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.08,
      "end_seconds": 241.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.49,
      "end_seconds": 258.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "There's tenderness in the lower tummy on the left, and no guarding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.74,
      "end_seconds": 260.44,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.72,
      "end_seconds": 274.95,
      "duration_seconds": 12.23,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Putting it all together, my working impression is chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis. It could also be a pelvic infection, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.0,
      "end_seconds": 278.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.78,
      "end_seconds": 302.5,
      "duration_seconds": 22.72,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis, and we'll know more once the a swab test is back. We should do a swab test for pelvic pain. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'd like to arrange a pelvic ultrasound for pelvic pain. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.59,
      "end_seconds": 307.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Uh, sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.81,
      "end_seconds": 332.4,
      "duration_seconds": 21.59,
      "text": "I'm going to order a pregnancy test, for pelvic pain. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. Let's use mefenamic acid, 500 milligrams, three times a day with food, for five days. You take it by mouth. It's for period pain. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.57,
      "end_seconds": 355.95,
      "duration_seconds": 22.38,
      "text": "A heat pad and some gentle movement help many people, and a pain diary helps me see a pattern. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. I'll also refer you to a gynaecologist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.05,
      "end_seconds": 357.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.06,
      "end_seconds": 366.34,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the pain becomes sudden and severe or you faint, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.23,
      "end_seconds": 369.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.21,
      "end_seconds": 371.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Come back after the scan."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.46,
      "end_seconds": 376.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.47,
      "end_seconds": 381.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "So, take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.91,
      "end_seconds": 390.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I'll get started on all of that."
    }
  ]
}